{"ts":"2026-08-25T18:00:47.818677944Z","author":"maw-security","event":"CommentAdded","data":{"comment_id":"th-2sp7qq.1","thread_id":"th-2sp7qq","body":"INFO: Security review — no issues. The PreOverwriteGuard change converts a fail-OPEN boundary (detector failure -> Proceed) into fail-CLOSED (Unverified -> bail), which is the correct posture at a destructive checkout: a forged index stat cache can make a status-shaped query report clean while on-disk bytes disagree with HEAD, so refusing when authoritative hashing cannot run prevents silent data loss. The sole production caller (sync/checks.rs) matches all four variants exhaustively with no fail-open wildcard."}}
